{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.DominationTowers","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.DominationTowers","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.DominationSqueeze"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ns_enstrophy_exceeds_dissipation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ns_enstrophy_exceeds_dissipation","kind":"theorem","line":215,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationTowers.lean#L215-L227","doc":"**q-NS blowup bound** (`rem:ns-surreal-bound`). The enstrophy cost of a\nstandard-scale singular deviation exceeds the dissipation budget.\n\nProves the remark's *inference step* only; the q-NS conjecture cone\n(`conj:q-aubin-lions`, `conj:ns-counterexample`, `conj:critical-exponent`,\n`conj:blowup-yekutieli`, `conj:regularity-breakdown`) is its premise set and is\nuntouched. Note those five classes are *not* hypotheses of this lemma — the\ninequality never depended on them; see the rewrite note in\n`appendix-surreals/surreal-squeeze.lean`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.pnp_simulation_exceeds_budget","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.pnp_simulation_exceeds_budget","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationTowers.lean#L203-L213","doc":"**P-vs-NP bound** (`rem:p-vs-np-surreal-bound`). For an NP-complete instance\nof size `n`, the classical simulation cost `2ⁿ·δₙ²·Ω_q` exceeds the mass-gap\nbudget `2ⁿ·Δ_q` available over the same Reeb period.\n\nProves the remark's *inference step* only. That remark is explicitly\nconditional on an independent non-compressibility conjecture for\n`BQP_q → P`, which nothing here establishes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.collatz_drift_exceeds_dissipation","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.collatz_drift_exceeds_dissipation","kind":"theorem","line":191,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationTowers.lean#L191-L201","doc":"**q-Collatz bound** (`rem:collatz-surreal-bound`). The accumulated\ncontact-volume deviation `V(δ) ≍ δ²·ε⁻¹` over one Reeb period strictly exceeds\nthe mass-gap dissipation `Δ_q ≍ ε³`, so no rogue orbit with standard-real drift\n`δ` can be re-absorbed.\n\nProves the remark's *inference step* only; the contact-boundary model and the\n`std`-of-the-skein-resolution assumption are its premises, untouched here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.squeeze_scaled","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.squeeze_scaled","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationTowers.lean#L183-L189","doc":"**Scaled squeeze.** Multiplying through by a positive standard factor\npreserves the inequality — the step `rem:p-vs-np-surreal-bound` performs with\nthe factor `2ⁿ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.squeeze_core","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.squeeze_core","kind":"theorem","line":175,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationTowers.lean#L175-L181","doc":"**Surreal squeeze (shared core).** Restated here so this file is the single\nplace the millennium bounds cite. Identical to\n`appendix-surreals/surreal-squeeze.lean`'s `surreal_squeeze`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.no_relation_of_grade_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.no_relation_of_grade_zero","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationTowers.lean#L161-L167","doc":"**Contrapositive — grade `0` certifies no relation.** A tower combination of\ngrade `0` has a non-vanishing leading part, i.e. `P(Vol) ≠ 0`. This is the\nusable test: compute the grade, read off non-vanishing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.relation_forces_positive_grade","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.relation_forces_positive_grade","kind":"theorem","line":153,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationTowers.lean#L153-L159","doc":"**A relation among the leading parts lifts the grade** — the direction\n`qou-7jok` needs: if `P(Vol) = 0`, the tower combination `P(𝔙)` is a pure\npositive-grade series, so the relation imposes conditions on the arithmetic\ncoefficients `κₙ` (`n ≥ 1`) rather than on the volumes. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.grade_pos_iff_leading_vanishes","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.grade_pos_iff_leading_vanishes","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationTowers.lean#L134-L151","doc":"**The grade sees the leading coefficient — and nothing else does.**\n\n`0 < ohtsukiVal κ ↔ κ 0 = 0`. On a polynomial combination of towers this reads:\nthe combination has strictly positive grade exactly when the relation holds\namong the grade-`0` parts (the complex volumes).\n\nThis is the separation the surreal prune shows is *unavailable* on `ℝ`, where\nevery non-relation shares grade `0`. Lifting to the tower restores it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ohtsukiVal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.ohtsukiVal","kind":"def","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationTowers.lean#L129-L132","doc":"Grade of an Ohtsuki tower, as its `ℏ`-coefficient sequence: the leading\norder in `ℏ = 2πb²`. Definitionally `jetVal`; named separately so call sites\nsay which object they mean. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.infinite_tower_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.infinite_tower_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":120,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationTowers.lean#L120-L125","doc":"**The infinite tower is non-zero.** The perpetual-obstruction statement in\nalgebraic form: a non-zero leading level cannot be cancelled by its tail. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.leading_survives_infinite_tail","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.leading_survives_infinite_tail","kind":"theorem","line":110,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationTowers.lean#L110-L118","doc":"**The leading term survives an infinite tail.**\n\n`val (a₀ + T) = val a₀` whenever every tail term — and hence the whole tail —\nis strictly deeper than `a₀`. This is `val_add_sum_eq` freed of finiteness:\nthe brane tower does not collapse onto its leading level. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.lt_val_of_deepTail","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.lt_val_of_deepTail","kind":"theorem","line":100,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationTowers.lean#L100-L108","doc":"**The infinite tail is deeper than `γ`.** The finite machinery plus one\napproximation step; no completion of `A` is required. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.DeepTail.approx","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.DeepTail.approx","kind":"theorem","line":98,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationTowers.lean#L98-L98","doc":"Truncations approximate `T` arbitrarily deeply. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.DeepTail.terms","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.DeepTail.terms","kind":"theorem","line":96,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationTowers.lean#L96-L96","doc":"Every tail term is strictly deeper than `γ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.DeepTail.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.DeepTail.mk","kind":"ctor","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationTowers.lean#L94-L94","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.DeepTail","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.DeepTail","kind":"structure","line":90,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationTowers.lean#L90-L98","doc":"**The tail is deep** — convergence in the filtration, with no topology.\n\n`terms`: every term of the tail sits strictly below grade `γ`.\n`approx`: finite truncations approximate `T` to arbitrary depth. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Domination.lt_val_towerTrunc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.Domination.lt_val_towerTrunc","kind":"theorem","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationTowers.lean#L82-L88","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.towerTrunc_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.towerTrunc_zero","kind":"theorem","line":79,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationTowers.lean#L79-L80","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.towerTrunc","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AlgebraicSubstrate.towerTrunc","kind":"def","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AlgebraicSubstrate/DominationTowers.lean#L76-L77","doc":"Finite truncation of a tower: `a 0 + … + a (n-1)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}